{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1785697198,"nonce":"UWnWmAGhcL+Irz8s3UaknuddoD8=","title":"Verified 2026-08-03 for the architect's decision that **object storage is a SOFT, RECOMMENDED requirement**: with it Scarab is fully featured; without it the Depot is a warm-only cache offering a bounded RECENT window, with every degradation disclosed rather than silent.","message":"**Matrix as measured (no object storage = `SCARAB_S3_BUCKET` unset; ONE knob drives workspace cold, logs AND artifacts — `config.rs:156`, `main.rs:162-178`):**\n\n| feature | verdict | evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| Step logs | **silently break** | separate ticket — the read path swallows errors |\n| Browse a past workspace | loud, WRONG CAUSE | `list_workspace` maps a missing tree to 404 (`lib.rs:3118`), indistinguishable from \"no such path\"; `available:false` only fires when NO root is recorded |\n| Rerun/retry an old run | **works, bounded — degrades correctly** | `CasSnapshots::snapshot_present` (`retention.rs:136-159`) is a real content probe; a definitive NotFound widens the rerun to `clone` and names the widened set. Caveat: probes only the ROOT tree, so root-present + interior-blob-evicted slips to the fetcher |\n| Resume after Depot restart | loud | `scarab-wsfetch` maps NotFound -\u003e `FetchError::Permanent` naming \"evicted, or the store was wiped\" (`bin/scarab-wsfetch.rs:300-304`) |\n| Skip-if-unchanged | **works** | `input_signature` is a sorted join of Postgres-held digests, zero content reads. BUT the skip carries the prior `output_snapshot` forward, so the DEPENDENT's materialisation still needs those bytes |\n| Artifacts | break with the pod | same store handle as logs (`main.rs:485,608`) |\n| Results | unaffected | `step_runs.results` JSONB |\n| Retention/GC | **degenerate — deletes nothing, ever** | warm-only skips the cold flush, so cold stays empty; the sweeper only deletes unmarked COLD objects (`retention.rs:214-230`) and nothing sweeps warm. Residue suppression IS correctly tier-aware |\n| Event log / history | unaffected | Postgres |\n\n**GAP 1 (L, gating) — warm eviction does not exist, by design.** `WarmTier` is a trait with no implementation (`tiered.rs:539-570`); the missing half is an **access index** (`touch`), because `list_objects` gives least-recently-WRITTEN, which is meaningless for immutable CAS content. The only instrument is a 60s `dir_size` gauge. `values.yaml:270-273` says it plainly: \"LRU eviction is NOT implemented yet... this number is the whole budget\".\nDesign: a **size watermark** (not TTL — the budget is space), LRU over a real access index, evicting high-water -\u003e low-water. **Pin set, in priority order:** (1) any fence with an unconsumed drain record or live write ledger (Depot-only systems of record for ~24h); (2) input snapshots of a NON-TERMINAL Run (the mark walk already computes this reachable set); (3) under warm-only, anything not yet superseded — there is no recompute path. Reuse `SnapshotFarm::evict`'s rename-then-check ORDERING discipline (`farm.rs:101-109`) but not its lease files (Export-only, going away).\n**Two doc comments encode assumptions warm-only falsifies and must change with the code:** `WarmTier::evict`'s \"Safe by construction: cold still holds them, so an eviction can only make a later read slower\" (`tiered.rs:567-569`), and `note_warm_write_failure`'s \"the snapshot IS durable\" (`tiered.rs:242`). Under warm-only, eviction is LOSS and warm ENOSPC means the snapshot is NOWHERE.\n\n**GAP 2 (S) — Browse must say \"evidence expired\", not 404.** One error-mapping change at `lib.rs:3118`.\n\n**GAP 3 (S) — disclosure is served but never rendered.** `output_durability` is plumbed end to end (column 0042, DTO `lib.rs:1007`, generated TS `api/schema.ts:1288`) and NO UI component reads it. Also `ui/scarab-web-ui/src/snapshot-retention.ts:129-131` now states a falsehood: the cache \"evicts on its own, which only ever makes a rerun slower, never wrong\".\n\n**GAP 4 (S) — ADR-0063 part 6's volume-identity marker.** Per-Attempt stamps cannot say \"the storage under this Depot is not the storage this database describes.\"\n\n**\"Recent\" as a PROMISE:** a disk high-water mark, not age or run count — the only bound an operator controls and the only one already measured. Lands as ADR-0065 `RetentionProfile`'s warm space budget. Absence rule: reuse ADR-0063's absence-is-authoritative VERBATIM; it already generalises (\"a volume's loss is not observable as an event\" is as true of the CAS as of logs).\n\n**CONTRADICTION to resolve in the ADR:** the Depot became a SYSTEM OF RECORD for drain records and write ledgers in `e58ce1f`, which contradicts ADR-0061's \"the service's volume is a cache\" (`0061:261-262`). Warm-only sharpens it: under warm-only the warm CAS is a system of record for everything.\n\n- [ ] New ADR \"Warm-only as a supported mode: eviction, the recent window, and Depot HA\", importing ADR-0064's `DurabilityTier` vocabulary and ADR-0063's absence rule unchanged\n- [ ] Amend ADR-0061 part 4 — its LRU deferral is superseded; LRU is now the gating gap\n- [ ] Amend ADR-0051 — its multi-replica story covers the control plane only","files":null}]}